WEBVTT

00:02.383 --> 00:04.177
KATARA: Water.

00:04.886 --> 00:06.429
Earth.

00:06.679 --> 00:08.556
Fire.

00:08.848 --> 00:10.683
Air.

00:11.309 --> 00:14.979
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.104 --> 00:18.816
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.359 --> 00:21.986
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.111 --> 00:23.404
could stop them.

00:23.530 --> 00:26.866
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

00:27.283 --> 00:30.578
100 years passed, and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

00:30.703 --> 00:32.622
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.747 --> 00:34.999
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:35.083 --> 00:37.710
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.835 --> 00:39.045
AANG: Oof!

00:39.128 --> 00:42.423
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:58.151 --> 01:00.111
( SNORING )

01:00.237 --> 01:01.696
( CHATTERS )

01:05.742 --> 01:06.868
( BUZZES )

01:08.119 --> 01:09.120
Eh―

01:09.329 --> 01:10.330
( SQUEALS )

01:10.455 --> 01:12.040
( SPITTING )

01:12.165 --> 01:13.792
What are you doing in my mouth?

01:13.875 --> 01:14.876
( PURRS )

01:15.001 --> 01:17.963
Momo, you need to be a little
more sensitive to my boundaries.

01:18.046 --> 01:19.130
Ah!

01:20.131 --> 01:21.216
Huh?

01:23.385 --> 01:24.427
( GASPS )

01:25.929 --> 01:28.974
Give up. You're completely surrounded.

01:30.725 --> 01:32.978
SOKKA: Come on! Come on, come on!

01:34.437 --> 01:36.064
My scrolls!

01:37.107 --> 01:38.566
My staff!

01:40.318 --> 01:41.361
Uh!

02:03.425 --> 02:04.467
Yip yip!

02:07.220 --> 02:08.221
- Ahh!
- Ahh!

02:08.346 --> 02:09.723
Wait, my boomerang!

02:10.849 --> 02:11.891
There's no time!

02:11.975 --> 02:15.562
Oh, I see. So there's time to get
your scrolls, and time to get your staff,

02:15.645 --> 02:17.063
but no time for my boomerang?

02:17.188 --> 02:19.024
- That's correct.
- Oh...

02:23.987 --> 02:25.989
Sorry about your boomerang, Sokka.

02:26.281 --> 02:28.616
I feel like I've lost part of my identity.

02:28.742 --> 02:30.493
Imagine if you lost your arrow,

02:30.618 --> 02:31.870
or if Katara lost her...

02:32.996 --> 02:34.539
Hair loopies.

02:36.791 --> 02:39.627
Here's your produce, pony tail guy.

02:39.753 --> 02:42.339
I used to be boomerang guy...

02:45.091 --> 02:47.093
Hey, Water Tribe money.

02:47.218 --> 02:48.470
I hope that's okay.

02:48.595 --> 02:50.555
So long as it's money.

02:52.807 --> 02:54.225
Have a nice Avatar Day!

02:54.351 --> 02:56.061
Avatar Day?

02:56.186 --> 02:58.229
You guys are going to the festival, right?

02:59.647 --> 03:01.399
( MUSIC PLAYING )

03:05.820 --> 03:07.614
There's a holiday for the Avatar.

03:07.739 --> 03:08.782
Who knew?

03:08.907 --> 03:11.659
Look! They made a giant Kyoshi float.

03:13.870 --> 03:15.789
SOKKA: And here comes Avatar Roku.

03:17.665 --> 03:21.252
Having a huge festival
in your honor is great, but frankly,

03:21.378 --> 03:23.213
it's just nice to be appreciated.

03:23.338 --> 03:26.633
And it's nice to appreciate
their deep-fried festival food.

03:26.758 --> 03:27.967
Aang, look!

03:28.176 --> 03:30.678
That's the biggest me I've ever seen.

03:37.560 --> 03:39.896
They have a torch. That's a nice prop.

03:40.021 --> 03:42.482
It's bright, dangerous... ( SNIFFS )

03:42.607 --> 03:44.067
Smells manly.

03:44.192 --> 03:46.403
But I'm not sure I could carry it off.

03:46.528 --> 03:48.405
Hey, what's that guy doing?

03:48.530 --> 03:49.781
( YELLS )

03:52.409 --> 03:54.285
CROWD: ( CHANTING ) Down with the Avatar!

03:54.369 --> 03:56.204
Down with the Avatar!

03:56.287 --> 03:58.373
Down with the Avatar!

04:05.713 --> 04:06.798
Uh! Uh!

04:27.152 --> 04:28.945
Where did you get these?

04:29.237 --> 04:31.364
What does it matter where they came from?

04:31.489 --> 04:32.657
Hmm...

04:34.576 --> 04:36.411
Mmm!

04:36.536 --> 04:38.037
CROWD: Down with the Avatar!

04:38.163 --> 04:39.831
Down with the Avatar!

04:41.791 --> 04:42.834
Uh!

04:45.795 --> 04:47.547
( CHEERING )

04:53.219 --> 04:55.972
That party-pooper's ruining Avatar Day!

04:58.057 --> 05:00.393
That party-pooper's my friend.

05:02.353 --> 05:04.272
It's the Avatar himself!

05:04.397 --> 05:07.525
MAN: It's going to kill us
with its awesome Avatar powers!

05:07.650 --> 05:08.776
No, I'm not, I...

05:08.860 --> 05:10.361
Aah! Aah! Oh, ho, ho!

05:11.738 --> 05:13.615
I suggest you leave.

05:13.740 --> 05:15.658
You're not welcome here, Avatar.

05:15.783 --> 05:18.411
Why not? Aang helps people.

05:18.536 --> 05:20.914
It's true. I'm on your side.

05:21.122 --> 05:23.333
I find that hard to swallow,

05:23.416 --> 05:26.336
considering what you did to us
in your past life!

05:26.711 --> 05:28.671
It was Avatar Kyoshi.

05:28.796 --> 05:31.883
She murdered our glorious leader,
Chin the Great.

05:32.342 --> 05:33.593
You think that I...

05:33.760 --> 05:35.220
Murdered someone?

05:35.345 --> 05:38.389
We used to be a great society
before you killed our leader.

05:38.515 --> 05:39.766
Now look at us!

05:40.141 --> 05:42.894
- Ah!
- Aang would never do something like that.

05:43.019 --> 05:44.604
No Avatar would.

05:44.729 --> 05:47.273
And it's not fair for you all
to question his honor!

05:47.607 --> 05:50.568
Let's tell her what we think
of the Avatar's honor!

05:50.693 --> 05:53.655
-( BLOWS RASPBERRY )
-( CHEERING )

05:54.989 --> 05:57.575
AANG: Give me a chance to clear my name.

05:57.951 --> 06:02.205
The only way to prove your innocence
is to stand trial.

06:02.539 --> 06:04.624
I'll gladly stand trial.

06:04.749 --> 06:07.001
You'll have to follow all our rules.

06:07.126 --> 06:09.796
That includes paying bail.

06:10.088 --> 06:11.339
No problem.

06:12.465 --> 06:15.718
How was I supposed to know
they wouldn't take Water Tribe money?

06:22.433 --> 06:24.811
So some people don't like you, big deal.

06:24.894 --> 06:27.522
There's a whole nation
of firebenders who hate you.

06:27.605 --> 06:30.316
- Now let's bust you out of here.
- I can't.

06:30.692 --> 06:33.194
Sure you can! A little... ( BLOWS )

06:33.319 --> 06:35.530
Swish, swish, swish! Airbending slice!

06:35.863 --> 06:37.073
And we're on our way.

06:37.323 --> 06:40.034
KATARA: I think what Master Swish
Is trying to say,

06:40.159 --> 06:42.620
is that you're supposed
to be out saving the world.

06:42.704 --> 06:44.581
You can't do that locked up in here.

06:45.081 --> 06:48.001
I can't do that with people thinking
I'm a murderer, either.

06:48.084 --> 06:50.420
I need you guys to help
prove my innocence.

06:50.795 --> 06:54.132
How are we gonna do that?
The crime happened over 300 years ago.

06:54.549 --> 06:55.758
That's okay, Sokka.

06:55.842 --> 06:57.510
For some reason, I thought you were

06:57.635 --> 06:59.220
an expert detective.

06:59.721 --> 07:03.308
Well, I guess I could
be classified as such.

07:03.433 --> 07:06.144
Yeah! Back home, he was famous for

07:06.227 --> 07:09.188
solving the mystery
of the missing seal jerky.

07:09.355 --> 07:11.691
Everyone wanted
to blame it on the polar leopard,

07:11.774 --> 07:13.610
but I figured out it was old man Jarco

07:13.693 --> 07:15.612
wearing polar leopard boots.

07:15.737 --> 07:19.240
See, a real 800 pound polar leopard
would've left much deeper tracks.

07:19.365 --> 07:21.618
Okay, I guess I am pretty good.

07:22.285 --> 07:23.870
So you'll help me with my case?

07:24.829 --> 07:27.624
Fine. But I'm gonna need some new props.

07:28.625 --> 07:30.335
I'm ready.

07:30.460 --> 07:31.461
( LAUGHS )

07:31.586 --> 07:32.587
What?

07:33.254 --> 07:34.339
( GRUNTING )

07:41.220 --> 07:42.347
Uh!

07:43.264 --> 07:44.307
MAN: Ah! Uh!

07:49.479 --> 07:50.563
Whew.

07:50.647 --> 07:51.648
Eh, ah!

07:51.731 --> 07:52.815
Ahh!

07:58.696 --> 07:59.864
Ohh...

08:02.617 --> 08:05.119
MAYOR: This is the crime scene.

08:10.416 --> 08:14.003
This is the footprint of the killer,
Kyoshi.

08:14.128 --> 08:19.550
It was at sunset, 370 years ago today,

08:19.676 --> 08:24.055
that she emerged from the temple
and struck down Chin the Great.

08:24.764 --> 08:26.641
After that tragic day,

08:26.766 --> 08:28.017
we built this statue

08:28.142 --> 08:30.812
to immortalize our great leader.

08:31.312 --> 08:33.481
Feel free to appreciate it.

08:41.948 --> 08:45.159
This temple and this statue
were cut from the same stone.

08:45.868 --> 08:49.080
And we know that the statue
was built after Chin died.

08:49.580 --> 08:52.208
So, if they were built at the same time,
that means―

08:52.291 --> 08:54.252
Shh! I wanna solve it!

08:54.502 --> 08:58.256
That means
Kyoshi never set foot in this temple.

08:58.339 --> 09:00.633
KATARA: That's a big hole
in the mayor's story,

09:00.717 --> 09:03.219
but it's not enough
to prove Aang's innocence.

09:03.636 --> 09:05.304
You're right.

09:08.141 --> 09:10.643
We need to go to Kyoshi island.

09:10.768 --> 09:12.603
Where'd you get that?

09:14.021 --> 09:15.106
( SNIFFING )

09:17.358 --> 09:18.651
( SQUEAKS )

09:18.776 --> 09:20.778
MAN: You got a bald head...

09:20.903 --> 09:22.447
Some nice tattoos.

09:23.906 --> 09:25.032
Argh!

09:25.116 --> 09:28.453
You're going to fit in
real well around here.

09:32.582 --> 09:33.708
( BELL RINGING )

09:35.376 --> 09:36.669
( LAUGHING )

09:39.213 --> 09:40.298
( GRUNTING )

09:41.549 --> 09:42.800
( CHEERING )

09:45.470 --> 09:46.471
Ohh!

09:46.596 --> 09:49.474
( EXCLAIMING )

09:49.599 --> 09:52.602
( SCREAMING )

09:52.727 --> 09:54.479
( SPUTTERS )

09:58.941 --> 10:00.568
Where's Aangy?

10:00.985 --> 10:02.361
He couldn't be here, Koko.

10:02.945 --> 10:03.988
ALL: Oh...

10:04.071 --> 10:05.615
I want to see Aangy.

10:05.740 --> 10:06.824
Oh.

10:17.168 --> 10:19.462
Oyaji, Aang is in jail.

10:19.587 --> 10:22.882
The town of Chin says he murdered
their leader in a past life.

10:23.007 --> 10:25.259
They say it was Kyoshi.

10:25.384 --> 10:27.762
Kyoshi? That's crazy talk.

10:27.887 --> 10:29.222
I'll take you to her shrine.

10:29.347 --> 10:32.517
Maybe something there
will help you clear her name.

10:34.936 --> 10:37.396
So, uh... What's Suki up to?

10:37.522 --> 10:39.106
Is she around?

10:39.232 --> 10:42.777
Actually, she and the other warriors
left to fight in the war.

10:43.319 --> 10:45.238
You kids had a big impact on Suki.

10:45.363 --> 10:47.198
She said you inspired her,

10:47.323 --> 10:49.784
and she wanted to help change the world.

10:50.117 --> 10:52.620
Oh, well... That's great.

10:54.622 --> 10:58.501
OYAJI: This temple was converted
into a shrine to Kyoshi.

10:58.626 --> 11:00.795
The clerics tell us these relics

11:00.920 --> 11:03.381
are still connected to her spirit.

11:03.506 --> 11:05.091
That's her kimono.

11:05.216 --> 11:07.885
- She had exquisite taste.
- Please don't touch!

11:08.010 --> 11:09.595
SOKKA: These fans,

11:09.720 --> 11:11.347
they were her weapons, no?

11:11.472 --> 11:14.684
Also refrain from touching the fans.

11:14.809 --> 11:18.020
These were her boots?
Her feet must have been enormous.

11:18.145 --> 11:19.272
( SQUEAKS )

11:19.397 --> 11:22.108
The biggest of any Avatar.

11:22.233 --> 11:24.902
Wait a minute, big feet?

11:25.027 --> 11:26.404
Little footprints?

11:26.529 --> 11:27.572
There's no way!

11:27.697 --> 11:29.156
( CLEARS THROAT )

11:29.282 --> 11:31.325
Special outfit, hat and pipe...

11:31.450 --> 11:33.786
These things mean anything to you?

11:33.911 --> 11:36.747
You're right. I'm sorry. Please.

11:37.331 --> 11:38.332
Aha!

11:38.457 --> 11:41.502
There's no way Kyoshi could have
made that footprint.

11:41.627 --> 11:45.298
And therefore, there is nothing
linking her to the crime scene.

11:45.423 --> 11:47.008
Brilliant, Sokka.

11:51.220 --> 11:53.848
This girl you're talking about,
she'll come around.

11:53.973 --> 11:55.474
You just gotta hang in there.

11:55.600 --> 11:56.851
You think so?

11:56.976 --> 11:58.102
- Sure.
- Yeah.

11:58.227 --> 11:59.270
You're a catch.

11:59.395 --> 12:00.438
I don't know.

12:00.521 --> 12:01.522
Hey!

12:01.647 --> 12:04.358
You're smart, handsome, funny,

12:04.483 --> 12:06.652
not to mention you're the Avatar.

12:07.194 --> 12:08.446
You guys are great.

12:08.863 --> 12:11.490
Don't be afraid to tell her how you feel.

12:11.574 --> 12:12.658
( SNIFFS )

12:15.077 --> 12:18.414
This piece is called
"The Birth of Kyoshi."

12:18.581 --> 12:22.209
It was painted at sunrise
on the day this island was founded.

12:22.335 --> 12:26.964
Why, it was today, in fact, 370 years ago.

12:27.089 --> 12:29.258
( SPITS ) 370 years?

12:29.383 --> 12:31.385
Wait, are you sure it was today?

12:31.510 --> 12:33.471
Well, seeing how it's Kyoshi day,

12:33.596 --> 12:35.598
yes, I'm sure.

12:36.474 --> 12:40.853
This ceremony didn't take place
at sunrise, it took place at sunset.

12:40.978 --> 12:42.563
Look at the shadows.

12:42.688 --> 12:45.983
They point east,
so the sun must have been in the west.

12:46.108 --> 12:48.277
- So what?
- Aah!

12:48.361 --> 12:50.279
If Kyoshi was in the ceremony at sunset,

12:50.363 --> 12:52.949
she couldn't have been in Chin
committing the crime.

12:53.532 --> 12:55.451
She has an alibi.

12:55.534 --> 12:56.869
Oh, uh!

12:57.620 --> 13:00.247
Honorable mayor,
we've prepared a solid defense

13:00.331 --> 13:01.332
for the Avatar.

13:01.415 --> 13:02.625
We did an investigation,

13:02.750 --> 13:04.710
and found some very strong evidence.

13:05.211 --> 13:06.963
MAYOR: Evidence? Ha!

13:07.088 --> 13:09.340
That's not how our court system works.

13:09.632 --> 13:11.592
Then how can I prove my innocence?

13:11.717 --> 13:15.304
Simple. I say what happened,
and then you say what happened,

13:15.388 --> 13:18.349
and then I decide who's right.

13:18.474 --> 13:19.558
-( GASPS )
-( GASPS )

13:19.892 --> 13:23.521
That's why we call it justice,
because it's just us.

13:23.938 --> 13:25.773
( LAUGHING )

13:32.613 --> 13:34.407
Everyone loved Chin the Great,

13:34.532 --> 13:36.325
because he was so great.

13:36.534 --> 13:39.495
Then the Avatar showed up and killed him,

13:39.704 --> 13:41.872
and that's how it happened.

13:42.081 --> 13:46.335
The accused will now present its argument.

13:47.712 --> 13:50.172
You can do it, Aang.
Just remember the evidence.

13:50.297 --> 13:53.426
Right... Evidence.

13:53.551 --> 13:55.094
Ladies and gentlemen,

13:55.219 --> 13:57.638
I'm about to tell you
what really happened,

13:57.763 --> 14:00.433
and I will prove it with facts.

14:00.558 --> 14:02.351
Fact number one:

14:03.394 --> 14:05.104
Uh...

14:05.229 --> 14:06.564
The footprints.

14:06.689 --> 14:07.773
Oh, yeah.

14:08.357 --> 14:11.360
You see, I have very large feet.

14:14.155 --> 14:15.448
Furthermore,

14:15.906 --> 14:19.118
your temple... Matches your statue.

14:21.203 --> 14:24.290
But I was in a painting at sunset.

14:25.291 --> 14:26.375
So there you have it.

14:26.459 --> 14:27.960
I'm not guilty!

14:29.754 --> 14:31.047
He's dead.

14:33.215 --> 14:36.135
Looks like you did some serious shopping.

14:37.053 --> 14:38.596
But where did you get the money?

14:38.721 --> 14:40.639
Do you like your new teapot?

14:40.973 --> 14:44.310
To be honest with you,
the best tea tastes delicious

14:44.435 --> 14:46.729
whether it comes in a porcelain pot,

14:46.854 --> 14:48.481
or a tin cup.

14:49.023 --> 14:52.276
I know we've had
some difficult times lately.

14:52.401 --> 14:56.030
We've had to struggle just to get by.

14:56.489 --> 14:58.491
But it's nothing to be ashamed of.

14:58.616 --> 15:01.952
There is a simple honor in poverty.

15:02.078 --> 15:04.747
There's no honor for me
without the Avatar.

15:04.872 --> 15:05.915
Zuko...

15:07.583 --> 15:10.544
Even if you did capture the Avatar,

15:10.628 --> 15:13.881
I'm not so sure
it would solve our problems.

15:14.006 --> 15:15.341
Not now.

15:15.466 --> 15:17.051
Then there is no hope at all.

15:17.176 --> 15:18.844
No, Zuko!

15:18.969 --> 15:21.180
You must never give in to despair.

15:21.305 --> 15:23.891
Allow yourself to slip down that road

15:23.974 --> 15:26.727
and you surrender
to your lowest instincts.

15:28.145 --> 15:30.022
In the darkest times,

15:30.147 --> 15:33.400
hope is something you give yourself.

15:33.526 --> 15:36.987
That is the meaning of inner strength.

15:46.580 --> 15:48.040
KATARA: Mayor Tong.

15:48.499 --> 15:51.001
I'd like for the court
to hear one last testimony.

15:51.460 --> 15:55.005
I've already told you!
It's just me and the accused.

15:55.131 --> 15:57.508
You can't call any witnesses.

15:57.633 --> 15:59.718
This isn't just any witness.

15:59.844 --> 16:01.554
I'm going to call...

16:01.679 --> 16:04.014
Avatar Kyoshi herself!

16:04.140 --> 16:05.850
CROWD: ( MURMURING )

16:05.975 --> 16:07.351
Are they serious?

16:07.434 --> 16:08.561
MAN: That's impossible.

16:13.566 --> 16:14.733
What are you doing?

16:14.859 --> 16:17.069
Well, she is Aang's past life.

16:17.194 --> 16:19.947
Maybe wearing her stuff
will trigger something.

16:20.072 --> 16:23.242
I do believe in the power of stuff...

16:24.034 --> 16:25.536
This is a mockery of Chin law!

16:26.120 --> 16:28.372
Please, if you could
just wait one more second!

16:28.497 --> 16:30.708
I'm sure Kyoshi will be here.

16:33.419 --> 16:36.630
( SPEAKING IN HIGH VOICE )
Hey, everybody. Avatar Kyoshi here.

16:36.881 --> 16:39.341
This is ridiculous.

16:39.550 --> 16:42.052
For the murder of Chin the Great,

16:42.261 --> 16:44.638
this court finds the Avatar...

16:55.316 --> 16:57.443
I killed Chin the Conqueror...

16:59.570 --> 17:01.280
A horrible tyrant.

17:01.405 --> 17:02.948
Chin was expanding his army

17:03.073 --> 17:05.242
to all corners of the continent.

17:05.910 --> 17:08.954
When they came to the neck
of the peninsula where we lived,

17:09.038 --> 17:11.081
he demanded our immediate surrender.

17:11.790 --> 17:15.794
I warned him that I would not
sit passively while he took our home.

17:16.378 --> 17:18.255
But he did not back down.

17:25.971 --> 17:29.516
On that day, we split from the mainland.

17:31.894 --> 17:36.565
( RUMBLING )

18:03.842 --> 18:05.719
Ahh!

18:07.221 --> 18:08.264
Aah!

18:08.389 --> 18:09.890
( SPLASHING )

18:12.142 --> 18:13.852
KYOSHI: I created Kyoshi island

18:13.978 --> 18:16.605
so my people could be safe from invaders.

18:24.780 --> 18:25.864
Oh...

18:27.032 --> 18:29.952
So... What just happened?

18:30.077 --> 18:33.163
Uh... You kind of confessed.

18:33.289 --> 18:34.707
Sorry.

18:34.832 --> 18:37.626
And I find you guilty!

18:38.419 --> 18:40.963
Bring out the Wheel of Punishment!

18:41.046 --> 18:42.715
CROWD: ( CHEERING )

18:42.965 --> 18:44.300
( CHATTERS )

18:48.304 --> 18:49.513
Uncle...

18:49.596 --> 18:51.348
I thought a lot about what you said.

18:51.682 --> 18:53.809
You did? Good, good.

18:53.892 --> 18:55.477
It's helped me realize something.

18:55.602 --> 18:58.647
We no longer have anything to gain
by traveling together.

19:00.107 --> 19:01.692
I need to find my own way.

19:09.158 --> 19:10.743
IROH: Wait!

19:10.868 --> 19:11.994
( GRUNTS )

19:25.090 --> 19:29.011
MAN: The accused will now
Spin the Wheel of Punishment

19:29.094 --> 19:31.305
to determine his sentence.

19:33.724 --> 19:35.559
I said I would face justice,

19:35.684 --> 19:36.685
so I will.

19:42.441 --> 19:44.276
Come on torture machine!

19:44.401 --> 19:46.070
Eaten by bears!

19:46.195 --> 19:47.488
Razor pit!

19:47.613 --> 19:48.655
Community service!

19:48.781 --> 19:50.616
Please stop on community service!

19:56.163 --> 19:59.375
Looks like it's boiled in oil.

19:59.500 --> 20:00.959
( CHEERING )

20:10.719 --> 20:14.431
We've come to claim
this village for the Fire Lord!

20:14.765 --> 20:16.892
Now show me your leader, so I may...

20:21.063 --> 20:22.481
Dethrone him.

20:22.940 --> 20:25.109
- That's him over there!
-( YELPS )

20:25.234 --> 20:27.277
You, Avatar. Do something!

20:27.778 --> 20:29.655
Gee, I'd love to help,

20:29.780 --> 20:32.074
but I'm supposed to be boiled in oil.

20:33.242 --> 20:34.701
There, community service.

20:34.827 --> 20:36.286
Now serve our community,

20:36.412 --> 20:38.414
and get rid of those rhinos!

20:42.501 --> 20:43.585
( GROWLS )

20:48.507 --> 20:49.591
Uh!

20:51.135 --> 20:52.177
( SPLASHING )

20:52.511 --> 20:53.887
( GROWLS )

20:54.012 --> 20:55.097
Ahh!

20:59.810 --> 21:02.187
Rough Rhinos, to the town!

21:02.312 --> 21:03.439
( SCREAMING )

21:11.697 --> 21:12.948
Ahh!

21:25.252 --> 21:26.336
( GASPS )

21:34.470 --> 21:35.846
Boomerang!

21:35.971 --> 21:38.348
You do always come back.

21:45.063 --> 21:46.106
Ah!

22:10.339 --> 22:11.423
Uh!

22:20.933 --> 22:21.975
Uh!

22:25.854 --> 22:27.481
MAYOR: From now on,

22:27.606 --> 22:30.150
we'll celebrate a new Avatar Day,

22:30.275 --> 22:32.361
in honor of the day Avatar Aang

22:32.486 --> 22:35.572
saved us from the Rough Rhino invasion.

22:35.697 --> 22:36.990
What is this?

22:37.449 --> 22:39.910
MAYOR: That's our new festival food.

22:40.035 --> 22:42.037
Unfried dough.

22:42.162 --> 22:44.331
May we eat it and be reminded

22:44.456 --> 22:49.878
of how on this day
the Avatar was not boiled in oil.

22:50.003 --> 22:51.463
( CHEERING )

22:56.760 --> 22:59.471
Happy Avatar Day, everyone.

23:03.767 --> 23:07.020
This is by far the worst town
we've ever been to.

23:16.446 --> 23:18.448
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
